From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:17:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: Settings > System > Reset root password, and root's
 password in the factory reset

Kiln OS keeps root's password on /data and lets the printer's own touch
screen set it back to "root" through its root update agent
(S68ad5x-update-agent, Kiln OS docs/helixscreen-integration.md, "Root
password reset"). This is the screen's side. HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds
only; other builds show nothing and keep upstream's factory reset.

The request. HelixScreen runs as root and writes
/run/ad5x/screen-request/root-password-default (root's folder, 0700,
which Moonraker, Klipper and plugins can't reach): the old
root-password-default.status deleted first, then one line, "reset
<stamp>" or "factory-reset <stamp>", the stamp CLOCK_BOOTTIME in whole
seconds when the press began, written under a mkstemp name (0600) and
renamed into place. The answer comes in the .status file ("done",
"refused: <reason>", "failed: <reason>"), looked for every 250 ms; the
agent's screen loop looks every second. After 10 s the screen gives up,
deletes its request so a late reset can't land, and says "No answer from
the system, try again". The agent's reasons are translated; any other
text (ad5x-passwd's own message) is shown as it is.

The button, above Boot into recovery. root-password-reset.state (a
plain file) says "unlocked" or "locked"; it is read when the page's
subjects start, every 2 s, at each press and after each answer.
Unlocked: "Reset root password", "Hold 5 seconds: SSH login root /
root", greyed during a print. Locked: a greyed row, "Turned off over SSH
(ad5x-passwd --unlock-reset)", which takes no press. No file (no agent):
no row.

The hold. LVGL has no 5 s hold, so the row's LV_EVENT_PRESSED starts a
timer that looks at the panel every 50 ms (ResetHold, no LVGL in it).
The press counts only when lv_indev_active() is DisplayManager's own
pointer (not the remote pointer, not an event without an input device)
and the panel is down on the row then; the hold follows the panel's own
state, not events, so HelixScreen 1.2's in-process Lua plugins can't
start or keep one. A lift of up to 200 ms (kCalibrationHoldGapMs, as
the hold to calibrate) is bridged; a longer lift, a slide off the row,
a scroll or the lock turned on ends it with nothing sent. A bar fills
over the 5 s with "Keep holding..."; at 5 s the request goes out with
the press's stamp ("Resetting..."), and the answer opens a dialog. The
hold fires once per press: no new hold starts until the panel has been
let go for more than 200 ms.

Factory reset. Its question adds "The root password also becomes
root." The press on its Reset button is stamped; perform_factory_reset()
resets and saves the config as before, then sends "factory-reset
<stamp>" whatever the state file says (the agent applies it even when
locked, and removes the lock), shows "Resetting...", then the answer's
toast for 4 s, and only then restarts HelixScreen. It is the only code
that sends "factory-reset" (a test reads the sources for that).

The texts in en, en-GB (empty) and de, es, fr, it, ja, ko, pt, ru, tr,
zh.

Tests: test_settings_kiln_rootpw.cpp (the state file's three states,
the answers and their texts, the request's line, mode and stamp, the
10 s timeout taking the request back, no folder, the hold's timing, the
indev check, the row unlocked, locked and locked during a hold, done
and refused, the dialog, one press one request, the factory reset's
request while locked and its stamp, the one caller, the texts in every
language) and test_settings_system_callbacks.cpp (the System page's
rows for each state).

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
